  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Reconciled all four St. Brigid discharges under RBC-TOC-02 and signed a progress note for each.\n\nWalter Kim (pt-0005): Furosemide raised from 20 mg daily to 40 mg BID (mr-t0001), using the signed addendum's correction. Potassium chloride stopped. Omeprazole kept (pantoprazole was only the hospital's formulary swap). Metoprolol XL, atorvastatin and aspirin unchanged. FLAG: The discharge summary said to restart lisinopril once creatinine was under 1.5. The 10/21 creatinine was 1.32, so that was met. But potassium was 5.4, so lisinopril stays on hold (§7). Task task-t0003 is assigned to you, due 10/26, for a repeat potassium. Note: doc-t0004.\n\nTerence Stark (pt-0004): Carvedilol (Coreg) raised from 6.25 to 12.5 mg BID (mr-t0005). Aspirin and insulin 70/30 18 units BID unchanged. FLAGS: (1) Atorvastatin 80 mg was filled only about 24% of the 180 days before admission, so I left it unchanged (§5b). Message comm-t0006. (2) He fills glipizide 5 mg from an outside endocrinologist (Dr. Desai). There's no clinic order and the discharge summary doesn't mention it. Not ordered. Message comm-t0007. Note: doc-t0008.\n\nAdelaide Thompson (pt-0042): Nifedipine ER (Procardia XL) raised from 30 to 60 mg daily (mr-t0009). Hydrochlorothiazide stopped, do not restart, per the signed addendum (thiazide-related low sodium). FLAG: Levothyroxine was filled only about 41% of the 180 days before admission (TSH 7.9), so I left it unchanged (§5b). Message comm-t0011. The discharge plan also asks for a metabolic panel at the follow-up visit and a TSH in 6 weeks; I didn't order either. Note: doc-t0012.\n\nEarnest Roberts (pt-0044): Restarted his held lisinopril 20 mg (mr-00373). The discharge condition (creatinine under 1.3) was met: 1.08 on 10/22. Latest potassium was 4.6 on 10/22, which replaces the 5.3 from 10/20. Rosuvastatin kept (the hospital's atorvastatin was a formulary swap, not ordered). Glargine and lispro unchanged. FLAG: He fills sertraline 100 mg from an outside psychiatrist (Dr. Nair). There's no clinic order and the discharge summary doesn't address it. Not ordered. Message comm-t0014. Note: doc-t0015.",
